<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-chile"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Chile.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Chile</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Democracy returns under President Patricio Aylwin</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-nicaragua"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Nicaragua.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Nicaragua</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Violeta Barrios de Chamorro defeats Daniel Ortega, ending the Contra war</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/principality-of-liechtenstein"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Principality%20of%20Liechtenstein.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Principality of Liechtenstein</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Liechtenstein joins the United Nations</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/russian-sfsr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Russian%20SFSR.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Russian SFSR</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The RSFSR declares state sovereignty on 12 June</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-lithuania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Lithuania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Lithuania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Supreme Council declares the restoration of independence on 11 March</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-latvia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Latvia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Latvia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Supreme Council declares the restoration of independence on 4 May</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/south-yemen"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/South%20Yemen.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>South Yemen</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Unification with North Yemen forms the Republic of Yemen on 22 May</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-yemen"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Yemen.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Yemen</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">North and South Yemen unite as the Republic of Yemen on 22 May</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/myanmar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Myanmar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Myanmar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The NLD of Aung San Suu Kyi wins an election the junta refuses to honour</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-south-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20South%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of South Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">F. W. de Klerk unbans the ANC; Mandela is released after 27 years in prison</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/anti-apartheid-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Anti-apartheid%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Anti-apartheid movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">F. W. de Klerk unbans the liberation movements, and Mandela is freed after 27 years</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/direct-democracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Direct%20democracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Direct democracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Federal Supreme Court orders Appenzell Innerrhoden to admit women to its Landsgemeinde</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/one-party-state"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/One-party%20state.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>One-party state</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Soviet Union amends Article 6 of its constitution, ending the Communist Party’s monopoly of power</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/hungary"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hungary.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hungary</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Free elections in May bring the Hungarian Democratic Forum to the head of a coalition; József Antall becomes the first democratically elected prime minister since the Second World War.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/federal-republic-of-germany"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Federal%20Republic%20of%20Germany.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Federal Republic of Germany</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 3 October after the Two Plus Four Treaty, the German Democratic Republic is dissolved and its five re-established states accede to the Federal Republic.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/saudi-arabia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Saudi%20Arabia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Saudi Arabia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After Iraq invades Kuwait, King Fahd asks the United States to intervene and allows American and coalition troops to be stationed in the kingdom; Saudi forces join the Gulf War of 1991.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/singapore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Singapore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Singapore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Goh Chok Tong succeeds Lee Kuan Yew as prime minister after 31 years; Nominated Members of Parliament are introduced the same year.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/rwanda"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rwanda.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rwanda</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Rwandan Patriotic Front, formed of Tutsi refugees, invades northern Rwanda from Uganda, beginning the Rwandan Civil War.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/socialist-federal-republic-of-yugoslavia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Socialist%20Federal%20Republic%20of%20Yugoslavia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The League of Communists of Yugoslavia dissolves along federal lines; multi-party elections bring separatist parties to power outside Serbia and Montenegro.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/tuareg"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tuareg.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tuareg</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After a clash at Tchin-Tabaraden, Tuareg in Mali and Niger rise and claim independence for their homeland</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/solidarity"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Solidarity.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Solidarity</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Wałęsa is elected President of Poland and later gives up the chairmanship of the union</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/velvet-revolution"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Velvet%20Revolution.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Velvet Revolution</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Czechoslovakia holds its first democratic elections since 1946</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/nelson-mandela"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nelson%20Mandela.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nelson Mandela</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">President F. W. de Klerk announces his unconditional release, and he leaves Victor Verster Prison on 11 February</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/haudenosaunee"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Haudenosaunee.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Haudenosaunee</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A dispute over land at Oka, Quebec, leads to the Oka Crisis</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/berlin"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Berlin.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Berlin</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Germany and Berlin are reunited, and Berlin again becomes the capital of the whole country</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/shanghai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Shanghai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Shanghai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Deng Xiaoping permits economic reforms and Pudong is developed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/cape-town"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Cape%20Town.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Cape Town</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Nelson Mandela speaks from the balcony of the City Hall hours after his release</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/ghost-dance"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ghost%20Dance.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ghost Dance</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Congress officially apologises for the Wounded Knee Massacre without rescinding any Medal of Honor</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/christian-democracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Christian%20democracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Christian democracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Corneliu Coposu re-enrols his party in Romania as the Christian Democratic National Peasants' Party</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/juche"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Juche.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Juche</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Kim Jong Il introduces Socialism of Our Style after the revolutions that brought down the Eastern Bloc</span></li></ul></section>
